      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the coefficient of ${x}^{2}y$ in the product $(x-y)({x}^{2}+6xy-9{y}^{2})?$",
      "worked_solution": "We distribute all three terms of the binomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-y)({x}^{2}+6xy-9{y}^{2}) & = \\\\ x({x}^{2}+6xy-9{y}^{2})+(-y)({x}^{2}+6xy-9{y}^{2}) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}y-9x{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}y-6x{y}^{2}+9{y}^{3} & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}y-15x{y}^{2}+9{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{2}y$ is $5.$",
