      "problem": "Given that  $({t}^{2}+t+2)({t}^{2}+2t+1)={t}^{4}+a{t}^{3}+b{t}^{2}+ct+2,$ calculate $a+b+c.$",
      "worked_solution": "We distribute all three terms of the trinomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({t}^{2}+t+2)({t}^{2}+2t+1) & = \\\\ {t}^{2}({t}^{2}+2t+1)+t({t}^{2}+2t+1)+2({t}^{2}+2t+1) & = \\\\ {t}^{4}+2{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}+t+2{t}^{2}+4t+2 & = \\\\ {t}^{4}+3{t}^{3}+5{t}^{2}+5t+2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,$ $b=5,$ and $c=5.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b+c=3+5+5=13.\n$$",
